 - **Bonus trade valuation uses `iAIObjective`:** In `CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal`, the AI now factors each bonus’s `iAIObjective` weight directly into price—higher-priority strategic bonuses (per your weights) command more value in trades.
 - **Era- & inventory-aware relative pricing for key strategic bonuses (Horse<->Camel, Camel<->Horse, ±Elephants):** Also in `CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal`, trade values now adjust by what the buyer already has and by era. Examples: Medieval buyer with **Horse/Camel** but no **Iron** values Iron ≈ x2 (to unlock Knights); by Renaissance that premium fades (Muskets don’t need any bonus; Cannons only need Iron). **Elephants** are valued in Ancient/Classical, but discounted in Medieval (≈ x0.5, for buildings at most). **Copper/Iron** are discounted in Classical if the buyer already has Camel/Horse/Elephants; Horse and Camel are treated as partial substitutes early on. **Update:** this adjustment no longer applies to trades *within* the same master–vassal(s) locus, since it is generally in their shared interest to strengthen each other.
-- **Do not buy dominated or equivalent strategic bonuses (era and bonus-aware):** strategic resource buying now uses explicit exclusion rules, so AI skips dominated/equivalent offers instead of considering them as valid buys. Examples: in Classical, Copper is not needed if we have Iron; in Classical metals and mounted lines can substitute each other so redundant buys are skipped; Horse and Camel are treated as equivalent in Classical/Medieval/Renaissance; in Industrial (before Modern), Horse has the edge (no Camel Dragoon), so Camel is skipped if Horse is already available, etc. Change in `CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTrade`. See [KI#109](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#109---tremendously-improved-ai-bonus-trading-ai-very-inefficiently-buying-dominated-or-equivalent-strategic-bonuses-era-and-bonus-aware-exclusions).
-- **Aggressive tech trade discounts for widely known techs:** AIs now sell technologies known by ≥1 of their rivals at **heavy discounts** (e.g. 25% of the original cost/value), recognizing that it is better to secure **some gold** immediately via a cheap sale than to hold out and risk getting **0 gold** if a rival sells it first; implemented in `CvPlayerAI::AI_dealVal`. To compensate for this higher trading efficiency, **AI research costs** (`iAIResearchPercent`) have been adjusted (reduced/increased at higher/lower handicaps). See [KI#83](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#83---tremendously-improved-ais-not-trading-techs-more-aggressively-and-cheaply-when-rivals-discover-them-too-and-there-is-a-risk-they-will-beat-us-to-the-sale-leaving-us-with-nothing-rather-than-little-gold-or-such-which-would-have-been-much-better).
-- **Preferential master–vassal tech trading:** Heavily increase willingness to trade techs with our **master/vassal(s)**; change in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo`. This synergises with the earlier "devalue techs your master/vassal already knows" change (see [Technologies (AI)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md#technologies-ai)) and extends it **to *all* techs**, not just techs that overlap with what our master/vassal(s) already know. In one autoplay sample this *seemed* to **reduce tech overlap** and **improve sharing** between vassals (who had many more techs) and their master (who now picks up more of them). Also updated `AI_contactRoll(CONTACT_TRADE_TECH` to pass an explicit probability multiplier (rather than relying on the default of 1), making tech-trade frequency more dynamic and tunable instead of solely personality-driven. See [KI#78](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#78---improved-trade-techs-preferentially-with-our-vassals-or-master-synergises-with-the-no-overlap-previous-master-vassals-tweak--add-a-second-parameter-now-ai_contactrollcontact_trade_tech-rcontactprobmult-to-have-a-more-dynamic-tech-trading-not-only-based-on-personality-according-to-chatgpt-51-and-then-corrected-by-claude-sonnet-45s-review-check-if-accurate). **Update:** Extend the same extra trade bias to **sibling vassal<->vassal** trades.
-- **Military-power–aware tech trade targeting:** If a potential tech-trade is *not* between members of the same master–vassal(s) locus, `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo` instead increases tech-trade contact chance toward **militarily weaker** players (safer, less likely to threaten us) and reduces it for **stronger** ones (less free value to future rivals). In one autoplay sample this seemingly produced a much closer game: the former runaway (Ewuare) was repeatedly caught up by rivals, and the game lasted to ~T419 instead of ~T288, with the lead changing hands several times. See [KI#80](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#80---tremendously-improved-ai-contacting-for-tech-trades-players-that-are-stronger-even-though-this-is-more-likely-to-be-detrimental).
-- **Master–vassal(s) locus first for tech trades:** Whenever the AI wants to contact other players for a tech trade in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doDiplo`, it now **first checks** whether the desired tech is already tradeable inside its own master–vassal locus (master, vassals, sibling vassals). If so, it **does not ask outside civilizations for that tech**, nudging trades to stay within the group instead. In one autoplay sample this *seemed* to help Ewuare win earlier by finally picking up the Dragoon-related military tech from a vassal, while the locus kept a similar overall tech pace to previous runs. See [KI#79](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#79---improved-before-contacting-other-players-for-tech-trades-first-check-if-we-dont-already-have-the-tech-in-our-master-vassals-locus-and-if-so-dont-contact-the-other-players).
